    {
      "id": 100683,
      "name": "Ameena",
      "username": "Ameena",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/{size}/1907_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-05-01T10:55:42.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Also, if something lets you use two powers in a turn, you can't use the same card's power twice. That is, if you have one copy of Stun Bolt out and can use two powers (in this case, quite likely considering this particular card is Wraith's so there's her lovely Utility Belt likely to find its way into play hopefully ASAP ;)), you can't use the Stun Bolt power twice. If you have <span class=\"bbcode-i\">two</span> copies of Stun Bolt out, however (as it's not Limited), you can activate both of them as they are two separate <span class=\"bbcode-i\">copies</span> of a card, therefore two separate powers.</p>\n<p>I think the only time when you can get around this is in the case of Mr Fixer (one of the Rook City heroes), who has a one-shot which specifically states he can use his base power twice that turn (note that if someone else lets him play this card on <span class=\"bbcode-i\">their</span> turn, he can use his power twice at any point during that hero's turn, because it specifies \"this turn\" so it's valid until that hero's turn is over and is separate from their own play/power/draw phases ;)).</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:29:04.045Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
